=begin
  Hold a stack of scripts and just run "";aesthene full" repeatedly, unless there is more than 1 word to pick from, then finish solving it and then continue.

  Improvement notes:
  Make script more efficient by whispering the first 4 guesses 1 at a time and stopping as soon as 5 good letters have been found or there is only 1 word left in the word list
  Make the first part of the script (redeeming, moving, touching, etc) more robust.  It should deal with running out of slips
=end

class Aesthene
  include DRC
  include DRCT

  def initialize
    arg_definitions = [
      [
        { name: 'check', regex: /^check/i, description: 'Check current lock' }
      ],
      [
        { name: 'full', regex: /^full/i, description: 'Redeem slip, whisper first 4 guesses, try to solve.' }
      ]
    ]

    args = parse_args(arg_definitions)
    check = args.check
    full = args.full
    @start_time = Time.now.to_f

